{
  "explanation": "The attacker attempted a credential stuffing attack by sending repeated HTTP POST requests to the authentication endpoint (/api/v2/session) from rotating IP addresses within the same subnet. The resulting '401 Unauthorized' status codes indicate that the login attempts failed, showing the authentication mechanism is currently rejecting the invalid credentials.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement rate limiting on the /api/v2/session authentication endpoint to restrict high-frequency login attempts.",
    "Block or challenge requests originating from the suspicious subnet range (89.248.160.0/24) using a Web Application Firewall (WAF).",
    "Deploy robust CAPTCHA or multi-factor authentication (MFA) on the login interface to mitigate automated bot-driven credential stuffing."
  ]
}
